# ID|CAT|Title|What changes|What to watch for|Compatibility (- = empty)
# UTF-8. English descriptions for the app; the CMD menu keeps using descr.ru. Commands live in tweaks.def.
PRIV-TELEMETRY|PRIV|Send less diagnostic data|Windows sends only required diagnostic data instead of optional data.|This does not stop all data sent to Microsoft. The data set depends on the Windows edition.|-
PRIV-FEEDBACK-NOTIF|PRIV|Hide feedback pop-up surveys|Hides Windows notifications asking you to rate the system or leave feedback.|Other app notifications stay.|-
PRIV-TAILORED|PRIV|Turn off tailored experiences|Stops Windows from using diagnostic data for personal tips and offers.|Regular tips and ads may remain: they have separate settings.|-
PRIV-ADVID-USER|PRIV|Turn off the advertising ID|Turns off your account's advertising ID that apps use to pick ads.|Ads do not disappear completely and may be personalised in other ways.|-
PRIV-ADVID-POLICY|PRIV|Block the advertising ID by policy|Stops apps from using the advertising ID for the whole computer.|The setting affects all users and may become locked in Windows Settings.|-
PRIV-ACTIVITY-FEED|PRIV|Turn off the activity history|Turns off the Windows feed of recent activities.|Continuing work across devices through this feed becomes unavailable. Newer versions may not have the feature.|-
PRIV-ACTIVITY-PUB|PRIV|Do not publish user activities|Stops apps from adding activities to the Windows activity history.|Related suggestions and cross-device continuation may stop working.|-
PRIV-ACTIVITY-UPL|PRIV|Do not upload activity history|Stops the Windows activity history from being sent to the Microsoft cloud.|Activities from this history will not sync between devices.|-
PRIV-INK-TEXT|PRIV|Do not collect typing samples|Limits collection of typed text samples used to personalise input.|Personal typing suggestions may become less accurate. The keyboard keeps working.|-
PRIV-INK-INK|PRIV|Do not collect handwriting samples|Limits collection of handwriting samples used to personalise input.|Recognition of your handwriting may become less accurate. The pen is not disabled.|-
PRIV-SIUF|PRIV|Never ask for feedback|Turns off regular Windows requests to leave feedback.|You can still send feedback yourself through Feedback Hub if it is installed.|-
PRIV-CONSUMER|PRIV|Block automatic install of promoted apps|Limits automatic suggestions and installation of promoted Windows apps.|Apps that are already installed stay. The policy effect depends on the Windows edition.|-
PRIV-SOFTLANDING|PRIV|Hide Windows tips pop-ups|Hides pop-up tips about Windows features.|Getting-started hints also disappear.|-
PRIV-LLMNR|PRIV|Turn off LLMNR (password capture protection)|Turns off one of the ways computers are found by name on the local network.|This reduces the risk of spoofed network replies, but old network devices may no longer be found by name.|-
PRIV-WER|PRIV|Turn off error report upload|Stops Windows from sending standard crash reports to Microsoft.|Diagnostics for some programs may become unavailable. Keep reports on while you investigate crashes.|-
PRIV-SVC-DIAGTRACK|PRIV|Stop the DiagTrack telemetry service|Stops the background service that collects Windows diagnostic data.|Some Feedback Hub and diagnostics features may not work. This does not turn off all telemetry.|-
PRIV-SVC-DMWAPP|PRIV|Disable the WAP Push service (dmwappushservice)|Disables the message delivery service used for remote device management.|Do not apply on a PC managed by an organisation. If the service is absent, the action is skipped.|-
PRIV-CLOUD-SEARCH-MSA|PRIV|Do not search the personal account cloud|Removes personal OneDrive and other Microsoft cloud results from Windows Search.|Files on the computer stay searchable. Cloud data can be searched on the website or in the app.|-
PRIV-CLOUD-SEARCH-AAD|PRIV|Do not search the work account cloud|Removes cloud data of a work or school account from Windows Search.|Use the organisation's website or app to search its documents.|-
PRIV-SEARCH-HISTORY|PRIV|Do not keep search history on this device|Stops Windows from remembering new search queries on this device.|Personal search suggestions become less convenient. This does not clear browser history.|-
PRIV-COPILOT-OFF|PRIV|Turn off Windows Copilot|Turns off the built-in Copilot pane where Windows supports this policy.|A separately installed Copilot app is not removed. Newer builds may ignore the policy.|-
PRIV-RECALL-OFF|PRIV|Turn off Recall (AI screen snapshots)|Stops Recall from saving new screen snapshots for searching past activity.|Only matters on devices that support Recall. This does not delete history already saved.|-
UI-FILEEXT|UI|Show file extensions|Shows file name endings such as .pdf, .jpg and .exe.|This makes it easier to tell a document from a program. Do not delete the extension by accident when renaming.|-
UI-HIDDEN|UI|Show hidden files|Makes hidden files and folders visible in File Explorer.|Do not delete unfamiliar files. Protected system files stay hidden.|-
UI-LAUNCHTO|UI|Open File Explorer to This PC|File Explorer opens on the page with drives and devices.|Quick access stays in the navigation pane.|-
UI-MENUDELAY|UI|Open menus faster|Cuts the delay before regular submenus open from 400 to 200 milliseconds.|Menus feel more responsive, but programs do not run faster.|-
UI-STARTUPDELAY|UI|Remove the startup delay|Removes the extra delay before startup programs run.|After sign-in, programs may load the computer at the same time. Overall startup is not necessarily faster.|-
UI-SEARCHBOX|UI|Taskbar search as an icon only|Replaces the wide taskbar search box with a compact icon.|Search stays available by clicking the icon.|-
UI-TASKBAR-LEFT|UI|Align taskbar buttons left|Moves taskbar icons to the left edge.|Works on Windows 11. Taskbar features do not change.|-
UI-WIDGETS|UI|Turn off widgets|Turns off the Windows widgets board and its button.|Weather and news in this board become unavailable. The widgets app is not removed.|-
UI-FEEDS|UI|Turn off News and interests (Windows 10)|Removes weather and the news feed from the Windows 10 taskbar.|On Windows 11 this item is skipped: the widgets setting is used there.|-
UI-CHATICON|UI|Hide the Teams icon on the taskbar|Hides the built-in Teams chat button on the taskbar.|Teams stays installed. Newer builds may not have this button.|-
UI-SPOTLIGHT-OVERLAY|UI|Hide lock screen hints|Removes some text hints shown over the lock screen background.|Automatic rotation of background photos stays on.|-
UI-SPOTLIGHT-338387|UI|Hide facts and ads on the lock screen|Turns off the extra feed of facts and offers on the lock screen.|Not every caption is controlled by this setting: the neighbouring item turns off other hints.|-
UI-TASKBARANIM|UI|Turn off taskbar animations|Turns off smooth taskbar icon animations.|Transitions become abrupt. A noticeable speed-up is not guaranteed.|-
UI-BING-POLICY|UI|Remove Bing web results from search|Removes Bing web suggestions and results from Windows Search on supported builds.|Searching for apps and local files stays. Use a browser to search the web.|-
UI-BING-USER|UI|Turn off Bing search (user setting)|Turns off Bing in search for your account on older Windows builds.|May have no effect on newer versions. In that case use the main item that removes web results.|-
UI-CORTANA-CONSENT|UI|Reset Cortana consent|Revokes consent for web search by the old Cortana assistant.|Only useful on builds where Cortana is still present. Copilot is not affected.|-
UI-CLASSIC-CONTEXT|UI|Restore the classic context menu|Brings back the full right-click menu without an extra click.|Restart File Explorer or sign out and back in. Support may change on newer builds.|-
UI-SYNC-NOTIFY|UI|Hide OneDrive and Office ads in File Explorer|Hides OneDrive and Microsoft 365 offers in File Explorer.|OneDrive sync is not turned off.|-
UI-SHOW-SECONDS|UI|Seconds in the taskbar clock|Adds seconds to the taskbar clock on supported builds.|The clock refreshes more often, which may slightly increase power use.|-
UI-END-TASK|UI|End task on the taskbar|Adds a command that ends a program to its taskbar icon menu.|Forcing a program to close loses unsaved work. Requires a supported Windows 11 build.|-
UI-COMPACT-VIEW|UI|Compact File Explorer view|Reduces the spacing between file rows in File Explorer.|More files fit on screen, but they are harder to tap with a finger.|-
UI-NO-RECENT|UI|Do not show recent files|Hides the list of recently opened files in File Explorer quick access.|The files themselves are not deleted. History in other apps stays.|-
UI-NO-FREQUENT|UI|Do not show frequent folders|Hides automatically chosen frequent folders in File Explorer.|Folders you pinned yourself stay.|-
UI-NO-TRACKDOCS|UI|Do not track opened documents for Start|Turns off tracking of recent documents for Start and taskbar jump lists.|Quick access to recent documents becomes unavailable. The documents themselves are kept.|-
UI-DARK-APPS|UI|Dark mode for apps|Turns on the Windows dark mode for apps that follow the system theme.|Programs with their own theme may not change. This is separate from the Wintools theme.|-
UI-DARK-SYSTEM|UI|Dark mode for Windows|Turns on dark Start, taskbar and other Windows elements.|The app theme is set by a separate item.|-
UI-TASKVIEW-BUTTON|UI|Hide the Task View button|Removes the button for open windows and virtual desktops from the taskbar.|Task View still opens with Win+Tab.|-
UI-COPILOT-BUTTON|UI|Hide the Copilot button on the taskbar|Removes the Copilot button from the taskbar where Windows shows it.|Copilot is not turned off or removed: there are separate actions for that. Newer builds may not have the button.|-
UI-START-RECOMMEND|UI|Remove tips and app promotions in Start|Turns off tips, shortcuts and new app suggestions in the Recommended section of Start.|Recent files and frequent programs are set separately. Supported on Windows 11 22H2 and later.|-
UI-START-ACCOUNT|UI|Hide account reminders in Start|Hides Start notifications asking you to sign in with a Microsoft account or finish setting it up.|The account itself and the sign-in method do not change.|-
UI-HIDE-GALLERY|UI|Hide Gallery in File Explorer|Removes the Gallery section from the File Explorer navigation pane.|Photos stay in their folders. The section exists on Windows 11 23H2 and later; the change shows in new File Explorer windows.|-
UI-NUMLOCK|UI|Turn on NumLock at sign-in|The numeric keypad is on right after you sign in to your account.|Takes effect from the next sign-in. On a laptop without a separate keypad, some letter keys may type digits.|-
UI-STICKYKEYS-PROMPT|UI|Do not offer Sticky Keys after pressing Shift five times|Turns off the shortcut that opens the Sticky Keys prompt after pressing Shift five times.|Writes the whole set of flags for this feature and turns off Sticky Keys if it is on; rollback restores the previous flags. Sticky Keys can be turned on in Accessibility.|-
UI-VERBOSE-STATUS|UI|Detailed startup and shutdown messages|Windows shows the stages of startup, sign-in and shutdown instead of a generic wait message.|Helps to see what slows startup down. The change applies to all users of the PC.|-
SVC-RETAILDEMO|SVC|Disable retail demo mode|Disables the background demo mode service for store display computers.|Do not apply if the PC is used as a store demo unit.|-
SVC-MAPSBROKER|SVC|Disable the offline maps service|Disables background maintenance of downloaded Windows maps.|Offline maps may stop updating. Online maps in a browser are not affected.|-
SVC-FAX|SVC|Disable the fax service|Disables the Windows service for sending and receiving faxes.|Do not apply if you use a fax modem or a program that depends on this service.|-
SVC-XBL-AUTH|SVC|Disable Xbox Live Auth Manager|Disables the Xbox Live sign-in service.|Sign-in and launching of some Xbox, Game Pass and Microsoft Store games may stop working.|-
SVC-XBL-SAVE|SVC|Disable Xbox cloud game saves|Disables syncing of game saves with the Xbox cloud.|Progress may stop carrying over between devices. Do not apply if you use cloud saves.|-
SVC-XBL-NETAPI|SVC|Disable the Xbox Live networking service|Disables the Xbox Live networking service.|Online play and other Xbox features may become unavailable.|-
SVC-XBOX-GIP|SVC|Disable the Xbox controller service|Disables the Xbox accessory service.|Controllers and accessories may not work. If a connected gamepad is detected, the action is skipped.|-
PERF-SYSMAIN|SVC|Disable SysMain (Superfetch)|Disables background preloading of frequently used programs.|Apps may start more slowly, even on an SSD. On a computer without a confirmed SSD the action is skipped.|-
PERF-WSEARCH|SVC|Disable Windows Search indexing|Disables background building of the Windows Search index.|Searching files, document contents and mail may become slow or incomplete. After rollback the index needs time to rebuild.|-
PRIV-TASK-APPRAISER|TASK|Disable compatibility data collection|Disables the scheduled task that collects program and hardware compatibility data.|The data helps Windows assess update compatibility. Restore the task if updates have problems.|-
PRIV-TASK-APPRAISER-EXP|TASK|Disable compatibility data collection (new name)|Disables the extra compatibility check task on newer Windows builds.|If the task is absent, the action is skipped. Roll back if major updates have problems.|-
PRIV-TASK-PROGDATA|TASK|Disable program data updates|Disables the scheduled task that collects data about installed programs.|This removes one diagnostics source but does not stop every way of collecting it.|-
PRIV-TASK-CEIP-CONS|TASK|Disable the Customer Experience Improvement Program|Disables the task that sends usage statistics to the Windows improvement program.|Microsoft receives less data for analysing how the system works.|-
PRIV-TASK-CEIP-USB|TASK|Disable USB device data collection|Disables the task that collects USB device usage statistics.|USB drives, mice and other USB devices keep working normally.|-
PRIV-TASK-DMCLIENT|TASK|Disable the feedback client|Disables the scheduled task related to Windows feedback requests.|Automatic invitations to take part in surveys may stop appearing.|-
PRIV-TASK-DMCLIENTSCEN|TASK|Disable feedback scenario downloads|Disables the task that downloads Windows survey scenarios.|New automatic surveys may stop being downloaded.|-
UPD-NOREBOOT|UPD|No automatic restart while signed in|Limits automatic restarts after scheduled update installation while a user is signed in.|This is not an absolute ban on restarts: update deadlines and other policies may take priority. Save your work.|-
UPD-DO-LAN|UPD|Share updates only on the local network|Allows update files to be exchanged only with computers on the local network.|Sharing over the internet is turned off, but traffic within your home or work network stays.|-
UPD-DEFER-FEATURE|UPD|Defer Windows feature updates|Turns on deferral of moves to new major Windows versions.|The period is set by the next item. The effect depends on the edition and update policy; regular fixes are not deferred by this setting.|-
UPD-DEFER-DAYS|UPD|Feature update deferral of 180 days|Defers major Windows updates by 180 days.|Use together with turning on the deferral. Actual availability depends on the Windows edition and policy support.|-
PERF-NETTHROTTLE|PERF|Remove the multimedia network throttle|Removes the network processing limit tied to multimedia.|Faster networking and lower latency are not guaranteed. Roll back if audio or video gets worse.|-
PERF-GAMEDVR-USER|PERF|Turn off game recording (GameDVR)|Turns off built-in game recording for your account.|Recording clips with Windows may become unavailable. This item is not meant for third-party recorders.|-
PERF-GAMEDVR-POLICY|PERF|Block GameDVR by policy|Blocks built-in game recording and broadcasting for Windows.|Recording through the Game Bar may stop working for all users. Games are not removed.|-
APP-NEWS|APPS|Remove: News (Bing News)|Removes the News (Bing News) app from your Windows account.|Its features become unavailable. Save any data you need first. Rollback works only while the app files remain on disk; otherwise it must be reinstalled.|If the app is absent, the action is skipped. Other accounts are not affected in normal mode.
APP-WEATHER|APPS|Remove: Weather (MSN Weather)|Removes the Weather (MSN Weather) app from your Windows account.|Its features become unavailable. Save any data you need first. Rollback works only while the app files remain on disk; otherwise it must be reinstalled.|If the app is absent, the action is skipped. Other accounts are not affected in normal mode.
