APP-PAINT3D|APPS|Remove: Paint 3D|Removes the Paint 3D app from your Windows account.|Its features become unavailable. Save any data you need first. Rollback works only while the app files remain on disk; otherwise it must be reinstalled.|If the app is absent, the action is skipped. Other accounts are not affected in normal mode.
APP-MIXEDREALITY|APPS|Remove: Mixed Reality Portal|Removes the Mixed Reality Portal app from your Windows account.|Its features become unavailable. Save any data you need first. Rollback works only while the app files remain on disk; otherwise it must be reinstalled.|If the app is absent, the action is skipped. Other accounts are not affected in normal mode.
APP-ALARMS|APPS|Remove: Alarms & Clock|Removes the Alarms & Clock app from your Windows account.|Its features become unavailable. Save any data you need first. Rollback works only while the app files remain on disk; otherwise it must be reinstalled.|If the app is absent, the action is skipped. Other accounts are not affected in normal mode.
APP-CAMERA|APPS|Remove: Camera|Removes the Camera app from your Windows account.|Its features become unavailable. Save any data you need first. Rollback works only while the app files remain on disk; otherwise it must be reinstalled.|If the app is absent, the action is skipped. Other accounts are not affected in normal mode.
EDGE-STARTUP-BOOST|EDGE|Turn off Edge startup boost|Turns off Edge preloading after Windows sign-in.|The browser runs less before you open it, but its first start may be slower.|-
EDGE-BACKGROUND-OFF|EDGE|Do not let Edge run in the background|Stops Edge apps and extensions from running after the browser is closed.|Background notifications and extension tasks may stop working.|-
EDGE-NO-DESKTOP-ICON|EDGE|Do not create an Edge desktop shortcut|Stops Edge updates from creating a desktop shortcut automatically.|An existing shortcut must be deleted by hand. The browser stays installed.|-
EDGE-TASK-CORE|EDGE|Disable the Edge update task (Core)|Disables one of the scheduled Edge update tasks.|The browser may stop getting security fixes on time. Other update mechanisms are not disabled by this item.|-
EDGE-TASK-UA|EDGE|Disable the Edge update task (UA)|Disables the second scheduled Edge update task.|May break automatic browser updates. Do not apply unless you are ready to keep track of updates yourself.|-
EDGE-UNINSTALL|EDGE|Uninstall Microsoft Edge|Tries to uninstall Microsoft Edge with Microsoft's own uninstaller.|Windows may block the removal. There is no automatic rollback: you will need to download and install the browser again.|-
SYS-POWER-SCHEME|SYS|Adjust power timeouts|On AC power the screen turns off after 20 minutes, and automatic sleep and disk shutdown are turned off.|The computer may use more electricity. Battery settings do not change; the previous scheme is saved for rollback.|-
SYS-HIBERNATE-OFF|SYS|Turn off hibernation|Turns off saving the session to disk and frees the space used by the hibernation file.|Hibernation and the fast startup that depends on it become unavailable. On a laptop the action is skipped.|-
SYS-FASTSTARTUP-OFF|SYS|Turn off fast startup|Turns off fast startup so Windows boots from scratch after shutdown.|This may help with driver problems or a second OS, but powering on may take longer.|-
SYS-LONGPATHS|SYS|Allow long paths (over 260 characters)|Lets programs that support it work with long file paths.|Older apps may still limit path length. Existing files are not moved.|-
SYS-TCP-AUTOTUNING|SYS|Reset TCP auto-tuning to normal|Restores the normal Windows auto-tuning of network receive data.|Useful after failed network tweaks. If the value is already normal, nothing noticeable changes.|-
SYS-LASTACCESS|SYS|Do not update NTFS last access time|Turns off updating the last read time of files on NTFS drives.|Backup and tracking programs that use this date may behave differently. The modification date is still updated.|-
CLN-USERTEMP|CLEAN|Clean user temporary files|Deletes temporary files of your account older than three days.|Files in use are skipped. Wintools cannot restore deleted data; close installers and apps first.|-
CLN-WINTEMP|CLEAN|Clean Windows temporary files|Deletes Windows temporary files older than three days.|Files in use are skipped. Do not run cleanup while programs or updates are installing.|-
CLN-CRASHDUMPS|CLEAN|Delete application crash dumps|Deletes old application crash reports from the CrashDumps folder.|Files older than seven days are deleted. If you are investigating crashes, keep the reports before cleaning.|-
CLN-DO-CACHE|CLEAN|Clean the Delivery Optimization cache|Deletes the cache used to share update files between computers.|Windows downloads the files again if needed. The freed space may fill up again over time.|-
CLN-WU-DOWNLOAD|CLEAN|Clean downloaded update packages|Deletes downloaded Windows Update installation packages.|Needed packages are downloaded again. Download services stop briefly during cleanup; the installed update history is kept.|-
CLN-CLEANMGR|CLEAN|Run Disk Cleanup with a safe set|Runs the built-in cleanup of temporary files, thumbnails and error reports.|The Recycle Bin, Downloads and the previous Windows installation are not in this set. Deleting the selected temporary data cannot be undone.|-
CLN-DISM|CLEAN|Compact the component store|Removes outdated versions of system components with Windows tools.|May take several minutes. Do not turn off the PC during the operation; a full component base reset is not used.|-
CLN-RECYCLE|CLEAN|Empty the Recycle Bin|Permanently empties the Recycle Bin of your account.|Check the Recycle Bin contents first. Wintools cannot restore deleted files.|-
PRIV-CDM-SILENTAPPS|PRIV|Block silent app installs|Limits automatic installation of apps suggested by Windows in your profile.|Programs that are already installed stay. Not every way of installing suggestions is controlled by this setting.|-
PRIV-CDM-SYSPANE|PRIV|Remove suggestions in Start|Hides app suggestions in the Start menu.|Regular installed apps stay in the menu.|-
PRIV-CDM-PREINSTALL|PRIV|Block preinstalled Microsoft apps|Limits adding of Microsoft-suggested apps in your profile.|Does not remove apps already installed or set this for all new users.|-
PRIV-CDM-OEMPREINSTALL|PRIV|Block preinstalled manufacturer apps|Limits suggestions of preinstalled manufacturer apps in your profile.|Does not remove software already installed or block the manufacturer's own installers.|-
PRIV-CDM-338388|PRIV|Remove ads in Start|Turns off one source of app suggestions in the Start menu.|Other recommendations may remain: they are controlled by separate settings.|-
PRIV-CDM-338389|PRIV|Remove Windows tips and hints|Turns off an extra source of Windows tips and hints.|There will be fewer hints, but this item does not turn off all Windows notifications.|-
PRIV-CDM-353694|PRIV|Remove ads in Settings|Hides some promotional offers inside Windows Settings.|Which blocks are hidden depends on the Windows version.|-
PRIV-CDM-353696|PRIV|Remove ads in Settings (extra)|Turns off an extra source of offers in Windows Settings.|Complements the neighbouring item: some promotional blocks are controlled separately.|-
PRIV-CDM-338393|PRIV|Remove recommendations in Settings|Turns off suggested content on Settings app pages.|Windows settings themselves stay available. Complements the two neighbouring Settings actions.|-
PRIV-CDM-310093|PRIV|Do not show the welcome screen after updates|Turns off the screen introducing new Windows features after updates and at sign-in.|Windows release notes can be read on the Microsoft website.|-
PRIV-CDM-SCOOBE|PRIV|Do not suggest finishing device setup|Turns off the screen suggesting to finish Windows setup and connect Microsoft services.|You can connect services manually in Settings.|-
SVC-WMPNETWORKSVC|SVC|Disable Windows Media Player Network Sharing|Disables sharing of the Windows Media Player library over the network.|TVs and other devices cannot receive it through this service. Local playback stays.|-
SVC-WALLETSERVICE|SVC|Disable WalletService|Disables the payment data storage service for Windows apps.|Wallet-related features of apps may become unavailable.|-
SVC-SEMGRSVC|SVC|Disable Payments and NFC|Disables the device contactless payment service.|Do not apply if you use NFC payments or related apps.|-
SVC-WISVC|SVC|Disable the Windows Insider Service|Disables the service for taking part in the Windows preview build program.|Do not apply if you want to receive Windows Insider builds.|-
SVC-SNMPTRAP|SVC|Disable SNMP Trap|Disables receiving service messages from network equipment.|Network monitoring programs may stop receiving alerts from devices.|-
SVC-MSISCSI|SVC|Disable the iSCSI Initiator|Disables connecting to network drives over iSCSI.|Such drives may become unavailable. If you do not know what attached drives are for, keep the service on.|-
SVC-PEERDISTSVC|SVC|Disable BranchCache|Disables sharing of cached work files between an organisation's computers.|On a corporate network downloads may become slower and use more traffic.|-
SVC-TAPISRV|SVC|Disable Telephony (TAPI)|Disables the service for phone lines and some modems.|Telephony programs and related hardware may stop working.|-
SVC-PHONESVC|SVC|Disable the Phone Service|Disables the service that manages Windows phone features.|On devices that support calls these features may become unavailable.|-
SVC-WPCMONSVC|SVC|Disable Parental Controls|Disables the service that monitors a child's computer use.|Family restrictions and reports may stop working. Do not apply on a child's computer with Family Safety.|-
SVC-TZAUTOUPDATE|SVC|Disable Auto Time Zone Updater|Disables automatic time zone changes based on location.|When travelling you will have to change the time zone by hand. Clock synchronisation is set separately.|-
SVC-PUSHTOINSTALL|SVC|Disable remote installs from the Store|Disables installing apps on this PC by a remote Microsoft Store request.|Regular installation from the Store opened on this PC is not disabled by this item.|-
SVC-ICSSVC|SVC|Disable Mobile hotspot|Disables the mobile hotspot service.|You can no longer share the internet from this computer through the mobile hotspot.|-
SVC-WFDSCONMGRSVC|SVC|Disable Wi-Fi Direct and projection|Disables the service for direct wireless connections between devices.|Wireless display and Wi-Fi Direct connections may stop working.|-
SVC-SCARDSVR|SVC|Disable Smart Card|Disables the smart card reader service.|Signing in and accessing work resources with such cards may become unavailable.|-
SVC-SCDEVICEENUM|SVC|Disable Smart Card Device Enumeration|Disables detection of smart card devices for apps.|Programs may no longer see an access card or its reader.|-
SVC-SCPOLICYSVC|SVC|Disable Smart Card Removal Policy|Disables automatic Windows actions when a smart card is removed.|The computer may stop locking when the card is removed. Do not apply on a work PC with such protection.|-
SVC-CERTPROPSVC|SVC|Disable Certificate Propagation|Disables copying certificates from smart cards to the Windows account.|Signing in to protected websites and work systems with a card may break.|-
SVC-SENSORDATASERVICE|SVC|Disable Sensor Data Service|Disables the service that receives data from device sensors.|Apps may lose light, position and other sensor readings.|-
SVC-SENSRSVC|SVC|Disable Sensor Monitoring Service|Disables monitoring of sensor reading changes.|Adaptive brightness and related features may stop working.|-
SVC-SENSORSERVICE|SVC|Disable Sensor Service|Disables management of device sensors.|Screen auto-rotation and other tablet and laptop features may become unavailable.|-
SVC-MSKEYBOARDFILTER|SVC|Disable Keyboard Filter|Disables the service that blocks key combinations in special Windows modes.|Do not apply on kiosks and terminals: users could bypass keyboard restrictions.|-
SVC-PERCEPTIONSIMULATION|SVC|Disable Mixed Reality simulation|Disables the service that simulates mixed reality devices.|Tools for developing and testing headset apps may stop working.|-
SVC-EMBEDDEDMODE|SVC|Disable Embedded Mode|Disables the service for special background scenarios of embedded Windows devices.|Do not apply on terminals and Windows IoT devices without checking their requirements.|-
SVC-NATURALAUTHENTICATION|SVC|Disable Natural Authentication|Disables the service that checks user presence through paired devices.|Dynamic lock and related presence checks may behave differently.|-
SVC-STISVC|SVC|Disable Windows Image Acquisition|Disables the service that receives images from scanners and some cameras.|Document scanning may stop working. Having a regular printer does not rule out a dependency on this service.|-
SVC-WIARPC|SVC|Disable WIA scan events|Disables handling of Windows scanner events.|Scanner buttons and automatic launch of the scanning program may stop working.|-
SVC-SESSIONENV|SVC|Disable Remote Desktop Configuration|Disables configuration of Remote Desktop sessions.|Connecting to this PC through Remote Desktop may break.|-
SVC-TERMSERVICE|SVC|Disable Remote Desktop Services|Disables the Remote Desktop service.|You can no longer connect to this computer over RDP. Do not apply during remote work.|-
SVC-UMRDPSERVICE|SVC|Disable RDP device redirection|Disables passing local devices into a remote Windows session.|Drives, printers and other devices may no longer appear in Remote Desktop.|-
SVC-BTHSERV|SVC|Disable Bluetooth Support|Disables the main Bluetooth support service.|Mice, keyboards, headphones and other Bluetooth devices may stop working.|-
SVC-BTHAVCTPSVC|SVC|Disable Bluetooth AVCTP|Disables handling of Bluetooth media commands.|Playback buttons and volume control on wireless devices may not work.|-
SVC-BTAGSERVICE|SVC|Disable Bluetooth Audio Gateway|Disables the voice connection service for Bluetooth headsets.|The microphone and call audio through such a headset may become unavailable.|-
SVC-SPOOLER|SVC|Disable Print Spooler|Disables the Windows print queue service.|Physical and virtual printers stop working, including printing to PDF.|-
SVC-PRINTNOTIFY|SVC|Disable Printer Extensions and Notifications|Disables some printer notifications and helper features.|Print status messages and extended driver windows may stop appearing.|-
SVC-PRINTSCANBROKERSERVICE|SVC|Disable the print and scan broker|Disables the broker between apps and print and scan devices.|Some Store apps may stop printing or scanning.|-
SVC-PRINTDEVICECONFIGURATIONSERVICE|SVC|Disable print device configuration|Disables automatic configuration of print devices.|Adding a printer and applying its settings may break.|-
SVC-FRAMESERVER|SVC|Disable Camera Frame Server|Disables the service that gives apps access to the camera video stream.|The webcam may stop working in video calls and other apps.|-
SVC-FRAMESERVERMONITOR|SVC|Disable Camera Frame Server Monitor|Disables monitoring of the camera service.|Webcam operation and recovery after camera failures may break.|-
SVC-QWAVE|SVC|Disable QoS for streaming media (qWave)|Disables the service that prioritises network audio and video.|Streams may become less smooth on a busy network. Faster internet is not guaranteed.|-
SVC-TRKWKS|SVC|Disable Distributed Link Tracking Client|Disables tracking of file moves for some Windows links.|After a file is moved, linked shortcuts or documents may not find it automatically.|-
SVC-SSDPSRV|SVC|Disable SSDP Discovery|Disables discovery of some media and smart devices on the network.|TVs, media servers and other devices may disappear from discovery lists.|-
SVC-UPNPHOST|SVC|Disable UPnP Device Host|Disables hosting of universal device network services on this PC.|Related programs and home network devices may stop interacting with the computer.|-
SVC-LLTDSVC|SVC|Disable Link-Layer Topology Discovery|Disables the computer taking part in building the local network map.|The PC may not show up in such a map on other devices.|-
SVC-FDPHOST|SVC|Disable Function Discovery Provider Host|Disables the service that finds devices and shared resources on the network.|Nearby computers and network devices may disappear from File Explorer.|-
SVC-FDRESPUB|SVC|Disable Function Discovery Resource Publication|Disables publishing this computer and its resources for network discovery.|Other PCs may no longer see it under Network. This does not guarantee that shared folders are closed.|-
SVC-WEBCLIENT|SVC|Disable WebClient (WebDAV)|Disables File Explorer and app access to WebDAV file resources.|Some network drives and work portals become unavailable. Normal web browsing stays.|-
SVC-WINRM|SVC|Disable Windows Remote Management|Disables the service that accepts Windows remote management commands.|Remote PowerShell sessions and an organisation's admin tools may stop working.|-
SVC-DPS|SVC|Disable Diagnostic Policy Service|Disables the Windows problem diagnostics service.|Built-in tools that find and fix problems may stop working.|-
SVC-WDISERVICEHOST|SVC|Disable Diagnostic Service Host|Disables one of the Windows diagnostics execution services.|Some troubleshooters become unavailable.|-
SVC-WDISYSTEMHOST|SVC|Disable Diagnostic System Host|Disables part of the Windows system diagnostics.|Automatic detection and fixing of problems may be incomplete.|-
SVC-TROUBLESHOOTINGSVC|SVC|Disable Recommended Troubleshooting|Disables applying recommended troubleshooting fixes.|Windows may stop fixing known problems automatically.|-
SVC-WERCPLSUPPORT|SVC|Disable Problem Reports Control Panel Support|Disables support for viewing Windows problem reports.|Viewing past crash details through related system windows may become unavailable.|-
SVC-WERSVC|SVC|Disable Windows Error Reporting Service|Disables the service that collects and sends standard crash reports.|There may not be enough data to diagnose program crashes. Third-party programs' own reports are not disabled by this item.|-
SVC-PCASVC|SVC|Disable Program Compatibility Assistant|Disables the assistant that offers fixes for old programs.|Automatic compatibility hints disappear. Old installers may need manual settings.|-
SVC-CDPSVC|SVC|Disable Connected Devices Platform|Disables the service for Windows interaction with connected devices.|Phone Link and data exchange between devices may break.|-
SVC-DOSVC|SVC|Disable Delivery Optimization|Disables the service that optimises delivery of updates and apps.|Downloads from Microsoft Store and Windows Update may break. To stop sharing over the internet, prefer limiting sharing to the local network.|-
SVC-DUSMSVC|SVC|Disable Data Usage|Disables Windows tracking of network usage.|Traffic statistics and limits for metered connections may become incorrect.|-
SVC-INVENTORYSVC|SVC|Disable installed software inventory|Disables the background service that tracks installed software.|Related diagnostics and inventory features may stop working.|-
SVC-DEFRAGSVC|SVC|Disable Optimize Drives|Disables the Windows drive optimisation service.|Defragmentation and scheduled SSD optimisation may stop running. Not recommended without a specific reason.|-
SVC-GAMINGSERVICES|SVC|Disable Xbox Gaming Services|Disables the services that install and launch Xbox games.|Game Pass games and some Store games may stop installing or launching.|-
SVC-GAMINGSERVICESNET|SVC|Disable Xbox Gaming Services networking|Disables the network part of Xbox Gaming Services.|Sign-in and online features of Game Pass games may stop working.|-
SVC-EDGEUPDATE|SVC|Disable the Edge update service|Disables the main Microsoft Edge update service.|The browser and related components may stop getting security fixes.|-
SVC-EDGEUPDATEM|SVC|Disable the Edge update service (second)|Disables the extra Microsoft Edge update service.|May break updates of Edge and related components. Manual updates may also need the service turned on.|-
SVC-WBIOSRVC|SVC|Disable Windows Biometric Service|Disables the fingerprint and face recognition service.|Windows Hello biometric sign-in stops working. Make sure you know another way to sign in.|-
SVC-WLIDSVC|SVC|Disable Microsoft Account Sign-in Assistant|Disables the Microsoft account sign-in service.|The Store, OneDrive and sync may stop working. Do not apply if you use these services.|-
SVC-WPNSERVICE|SVC|Disable the push notification system|Disables the app notification delivery service.|You may miss messages, reminders and other notifications.|-
SVC-RASMAN|SVC|Disable Remote Access Connection Manager|Disables the service that manages remote network connections.|Built-in VPN connections and programs using this service may stop working.|-
SVC-SHAREDACCESS|SVC|Disable Internet Connection Sharing (ICS)|Disables Windows internet connection sharing.|The mobile hotspot and WSL or Hyper-V virtual networks may stop working.|-
